The thing that actually worries me

Your VQA adapter has never seen a SAR image. VRSBench is optical RGB aerial imagery. SAR is speckled, single-channel, decibel-scaled, with inverted semantics — water is dark, buildings are bright from double-bounce. That is far outside the adapter's training distribution.

The ISRO/SAC evaluation set is "Cartosat-2S optical and RISAT SAR image pairs." Half of it is SAR. Right now your only real SAR capability is the deterministic sar_analysis.py percentile classifier — which is genuinely useful and physically motivated, but it isn't a vision-language model and can't answer arbitrary questions.

The fix is a third adapter trained on BigEarthNet-MM, which ships real co-registered Sentinel-1 SAR + Sentinel-2 optical with text annotations. That single dataset closes the SAR gap, the cross-modal gap, and the "BigEarthNet is the primary dataset" gap at once. It's roughly one more data-prep script plus one more Colab run — reusing the pipeline you already have.

